From 04698bfc53e104311bd091aef97e12a19460468a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:23:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] live switches host_rt_in_place and
 shadow_compressed for textures over host pages

host_rt_in_place (default off): under HostPageTexturePolicy::InPlace, a
texture over host pages whose usage renders into it or writes it is the
image in place (as a sampled one is), where the device's render-target
check passed for the pages' class (host_rt.rs). The check, per class, on
a thread of its own (started as the device is made where the switch is
on, else waited for, up to 5 s, by the first texture that asks): a
pattern in the pages, a texture of RenderTarget|ShaderRead over them,
then one internal submission making the image's first move from
UNDEFINED, a LOAD/STORE pass with vkCmdClearAttachments of a rectangle,
a CLEAR-load pass over a second render area and a DONT_CARE-load pass
over a third, all in GENERAL, while a thread writes every non-texel byte
(row padding, bytes after the image); every byte must read as due. Six
shapes (1/4/8/16-byte texels, padded and packed rows, 3440x1440 at a
13824-byte pitch), twice each. On ANV 26.2.4 (Arrow Lake): Pointer and
Fresh pass in 0.25 s, DmaBuf unchecked. The image tries the feedback
loop plan, then the undeclared usage, then the texture's own, as a
linear alias over the runtime's own buffer does. host_rt_max_texels
keeps larger textures shadows. Under the switch an image use of a key
over host pages takes the uses of all the key's bytes in
host_aliases::augmented, so an in-place write orders against other
imports of the same pages.

shadow_compressed (default off): a shadow planned mutable to any format
(PixelFormatView usage) takes the format list of the texture's own
views, so ANV may give it CCS_E. A RenderTarget|ShaderRead shadow is
CCS-eligible already (MUTABLE with B8G8R8A8_UNORM, _SRGB, R8G8B8A8_UINT,
exclusive, optimal, no ALIAS/HOST_TRANSFER/external): the switch changes
nothing there.

M2V_SHADOW_PLANS prints each shadow's plan (diagnostic).
M2V_LANE_IN_PLACE=1 gives lane devices the product's in-place policy.
host_rt_frames.rs measures frames under each setting, plus a clear
probe. live::set overrides a switch in-process. api_signatures.tsv
re-blessed (Device::settle_host_rt_checks, host_rt_check_report,
live::set).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
